[1mEverything else already matched.[22m The translation had faithfully preserved the C quirks that a naive port would "clean up" — I verified each against the C binary rather than assuming:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mif (c == '/' && (peek_char() == '/' || peek_char() == '*'))[0m calls [38;5;10mpeek_char()[0m before consuming, so it still returns [38;5;10mc[0m and the condition collapses to [38;5;10mc == '/'[0m. Every slash starts a comment; division is never an operator.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10manalyze_text[0m tallies newlines into [38;5;10mline_count[0m and then overwrites it with the tokenizer's never-reset process-wide total.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mtoken.column = current_column - token.length[0m mixes [38;5;10mint[0m and [38;5;10msize_t[0m, so a block comment spanning newlines reports a negative column ([38;5;10mLine 2, Column -2[0m).[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcount++[0m precedes [38;5;10mif (count > 100)[0m, so 101 tokens print before the truncation notice.[0m[0m
- A file of exactly 8192 bytes slips past [38;5;10mread_file[0m's [38;5;10m>[0m check and then fails the tokenizer's [38;5;10m>=[0m check, emitting two stderr lines; 8193 bytes emits only one.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msscanf("%d")[0m saturates via [38;5;10mstrtol[0m then truncates to [38;5;10mint[0m, so [38;5;10m4294967303[0m is read as [38;5;10m7[0m and actually exits.[0m[0m
